 "description": "Two chunks found in the bucket are promoted in one READ, but another process deletes the second object before the READ runs: NIXL fails the transfer as a whole, so unlike the fs tier neither chunk is kept, both slots are freed and both cached verdicts become misses. The verdict is per key, shared by every request holding it: a second request also gets MISS while the first holds it. Once both finish, a third request probes the bucket again and finds the first chunk.",
